# Lucy in the Sky with Diamonds, verse (figure 108.2)
# Two long vocal phrases over four backing phrases of 4, 5, 4 and 6 bars (Pollack's "4/5/4/6"
# phrasing); the typed systems are kept: 4 | 4+1 | 4 | 4+2. The bassline is the descending A G F# F
# of the intro ostinato (fig. 108.1); the second phrase ends with a move to F ("F-nat C F"), the
# fourth spells out D Major (F# A F# | A F# A | D) and descends through D to C, the V of the bridge's
# B-flat. Melody notes are one to a beat (3/4).
# Added: the melody's blank bars are shown as the last note held ("-"); Pollack leaves them empty.
# Changed: the third bass note of the fourth phrase's third bar is typed "F" but the essay's last
# section spells this lick "| F# - A - F# | A - F# - A | D", so it is written F#.
#? Bar 3 of the fifth system: typed "F# A F", read as F# A F# per the essay; check the record.
#? Phrases 2 and 3 start the bass on E (typed), not A as phrase 1 does; check it isn't a typo.
#? Octaves (melody C#5, bass A2 and below) are a guess for register.
